          "message": {
            "markdown": "\`ALTER TABLE\` waits for a heavy lock (\`ACCESS EXCLUSIVE\` or \`SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE\`) on \`orders\` with \`lock_timeout\` at its default of 0 (wait forever): it queues behind any long transaction, and every query that arrives after it queues behind the DDL. Run \`SET lock_timeout = '2s'\` (or \`SET LOCAL\` inside the transaction) before the first DDL and retry on SQLSTATE \`55P03\`. Not needed when your migration runner sets \`lock_timeout\` for every session: say so with \`lock_timeout_set_by_runner: true\` in \`.lurie-guard.yml\`. (PG004, [evidence](https://github.com/rafapeixer/db-skills/blob/c6eb44e9ab3b9458099b0a808ca4a2cde9f2db57/skills/pg-online-migrations/examples/bad/test.sql#L24-L49))",
