          "message": {
            "markdown": "\`ADD FOREIGN KEY\` validates every row of \`orders\` while it holds \`SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE\` on \`orders\` and on \`accounts\`: writes on both tables wait for the whole scan. Add it with \`NOT VALID\` (catalog only), then \`ALTER TABLE orders VALIDATE CONSTRAINT orders_account_id_fkey\` in a separate transaction, which takes only \`SHARE UPDATE EXCLUSIVE\` and lets writes continue. Not needed if \`orders\` is new in this release or empty. (PG008, [evidence](https://github.com/rafapeixer/db-skills/blob/c6eb44e9ab3b9458099b0a808ca4a2cde9f2db57/skills/pg-online-migrations/examples/bad/test.sql#L69-L85))",
